BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AAJA’s New.Now.Next Media Conference 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260523T000000
UID:be30d6050766e954b699fea6a62b9805@solutionsjournalism.org
DESCRIPTION:Bangkok\, Thailand\nThe AAJA-Asia N3Con returns to Bangkok. On
  May 22\, Kyuwon Lee\, SJN's training and curriculum manager\, will host t
 he panel discussion “Stories for Impact and Change: Insights from Field 
 Experts in Solutions Journalism” with journalist and trainer Anupama Cha
 ndrasekaran and journalist Nithin Coca.
LOCATION:Bangkok\, Thailand
URL:https://www.n3con.com/2026/
X-SOURCE:Solutions Journalism Network
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Covering the Planet with the Tools That Tax It: AI for Climate\, S
 cience and Environmental Journalists
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T000000
UID:3cc7ebffa03e25798c7ec36852a0625e@solutionsjournalism.org
DESCRIPTION:Online\nAI is both a tool transforming newsrooms and a story-s
 haping force in public life. How should journalists approach both with rig
 or?\nJoin us for a one-hour session with journalist and SF State Universit
 y Professor Yumi Wilson. We'll talk about AI using the solutions journalis
 m framework. We'll examine what AI actually does in newsrooms (response)\,
  what the evidence shows about its costs and benefits (evidence)\, what re
 porters are learning about its best uses (insight) and where AI falls shor
 t (limitations). You'll come away with a clearer understanding of how AI i
 s shaping journalism worldwide and a practical prompting structure you can
  start using on the beat.
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://uri-edu.zoom.us/meeting/register/5BFu_GsqT3qDJjYz_ijy0g
X-SOURCE:Solutions Journalism Network
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Find Your People: Engagement Strategies for Bringing Solutions Rep
 orting to the Community
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T000000
UID:d3094fd055ff60c4c482785c44bb6ec8@solutionsjournalism.org
DESCRIPTION:Online\nThere is sometimes a gulf in reporting: Whether due to
  trust or access\, the people most in need of the information can struggle
  to obtain it. SomeAdvancing Democracy granteeshave been addressing that i
 n creative ways. You can learn from them at “Find your people: Engagemen
 t strategies for bringing solutions reporting to the community.”\nWe’v
 e got two sessions\, May 7 and May 21\, each featuring two different newsr
 ooms finding success with including the public in solutions journalism. An
 d we’ll help you build your own road map for meaningful engagement — n
 ot just adding to your reach\, but building real relationships. You can si
 gn up for one or both.\nPart one — May 7: Gulf States Newsroom and Factc
 hequeado share how they embedded community listening into their solutions 
 reporting for the first time.\nPart two — May 21: Crosswinds News and Te
 xas Standard discuss building on prior solutions journalism training to de
 epen engagement on Native inclusion and adult education beats.
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://us06web.zoom.us/meeting/register/5-jrs4mPSyezTFfrCwoPdw?mc_cid
 =9d4c8b8c83&mc_eid=f6b9d64e2d#/registration
X-SOURCE:Solutions Journalism Network
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:National Geographic's Illuminating Climate Solutions
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260525T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260525T000000
UID:2c213ec949ea66f198838ca8d0630e4b@solutionsjournalism.org
DESCRIPTION:National Geographic has teamed up with The Climate Pledge for 
 a new storytelling fund. The goal is to “support a global community of E
 xplorers producing a portfolio of projects focused on climate resilience a
 nd solutions\, creating a stunning storytelling legacy that will inspire b
 usiness leaders and policymakers to take action toward a better world.” 
 Far be it from us to argue with that. The amounts offered are hefty\, and 
 so are the details\, so learn more and apply by May 25.
URL:https://www.nationalgeographic.org/society/grants-and-investments/rfp-
 illuminating-climate-solutions/
X-SOURCE:Solutions Journalism Network
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Association of Health Care Journalists' Health Journalism Conferen
 ce '26
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260527T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260530T000000
UID:192113c94f69cd7d17b3b192ff526ffd@solutionsjournalism.org
DESCRIPTION:Minneapolis\, Minnesota\, United States\nJoin the Association 
 of Health Care Journalists in Minneapolis for several days of field trips\
 , sessions and networking opportunities. Be sure to mark your calendar for
  the hands-on workshop "Covering Health Disparities From a Solutions Journ
 alism Lens" with Nora Hertel\, executive director of Project Optimist\, an
 d SJN's Wilson Liévano. You'll learn how to recognize leads that can turn
  into solutions stories and how to apply solutions journalism's four pilla
 rs framework. The workshop will be on May 28 from 8:30 a.m. to 10:00 a.m.
LOCATION:Minneapolis\, Minnesota\, United States
URL:https://healthjournalism.org/training-events/health-journalism-2026/
X-SOURCE:Solutions Journalism Network
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:⭐ APPLY NOW: Train-the-Trainers (July 2026 Cohort)
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260607T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260607T000000
UID:fa17565b28f84d4130002c848d07dcce@solutionsjournalism.org
DESCRIPTION:Online\nA new round of the SJN’s Train-the-Trainers program 
 is open now. For those accepted\, you’ll get extensive solutions journal
 ism training over the course of five sessions in July. That training will 
 deeply cover the fundamentals of solutions journalism before exploring bes
 t practices in teaching and training others in it.\nThe hosts for this rou
 nd will be Kyuwon Lee and Sharon Bloyd-Peshkin\, SJN's Training & Curricul
 um Managers\, and Raoul Junior Lorfils\, an accredited trainer in Haiti an
 d Canada. We'll also be joined by multiple SJN staff members and accomplis
 hed trainers from our network\, who will provide insight into their work i
 n solutions journalism. The deadline to apply is June 7\, soget all the de
 tails\, timing\, requirements and the full application all in one place.
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfQVupQXrW1bCkdvveBHVJyPmz6Ra
 VtG69TQDnKLtPHKZuVIA/viewform
X-SOURCE:Solutions Journalism Network
END:VEVENT
