BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Solutions Journalism Without Borders in Guatemala
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260614T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260614T000000
UID:7c5848ede36ccdc8af6083c615e7c87a@solutionsjournalism.org
DESCRIPTION:Guatemala\nBorn of an SJN fellowship\, Solutions Journalism Wi
 thout Borders is the only solutions journalism study abroad program. It wa
 s founded by Stephanie Jane Capper with the goal of helping train journali
 sts in locations often seen through the lens of problems. Now\, its next r
 ound of training has been planned: This immersive\, one-month excursion is
  happening June 14 - July 13 near Guatemala’s Lake Atitlan. Applications
  are now open\, sobrowse the details on accommodation\, training and more.
LOCATION:Guatemala
URL:https://www.solutionsjournalismwithoutborders.com/guatemala-program-20
 26
X-SOURCE:Solutions Journalism Network
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monthly Introduction to Solutions Journalism Webinar: June
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260616T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260616T000000
UID:60e1ae578bc4fe4fb86b1e014b2b2dad@solutionsjournalism.org
DESCRIPTION:Online (Zoom)\nThis one-hour Solutions Journalism Network webi
 nar will explore the principles and pillars of solutions journalism. We wi
 ll discuss its importance\, outline key steps for reporting a solutions st
 ory\, and share tips and resources for journalists investigating responses
  to social problems. We will also introduce additional resources\, such as
  the Solutions Story Tracker\, a database with over 17\,000 stories tagged
  by beat\, publication\, author\, location and more\, along with a virtual
  heat map highlighting successful efforts worldwide.\nThis training will b
 e led by SJN's Nina Fasciaux and Sarah ET Robbins from NPR.\nNote: This 
 event has been rescheduled from June 2 to June 16.
LOCATION:Online (Zoom)
URL:https://us06web.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_gprWuTStQuCfSolCUzOSsw
X-SOURCE:Solutions Journalism Network
END:VEVENT
